# Overview

Use Conventional Commit subjects:

```text
<type>(<optional-scope>): <subject>
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`,
`chore`, and `ci`.

## Scope (recommended)

The scope should indicate the area of the codebase affected:
- Module name (e.g., `auth`, `profile`, `events`)
- Feature name (e.g., `notifications`, `payments`)
- Component name (e.g., `HomeViewController`, `EventCell`)

## Subject (required)

- Use imperative mood: "add" not "added" or "adds"
- Don't capitalize first letter
- No period (.) at the end
- Limit to 50 characters

## Body (optional)

- Explain the "what" and "why" vs. "how"
- Use imperative mood
- Wrap at 72 characters
- Separate from subject with blank line

## Verification

- Every commit must pass the formatting and linting pre-commit hook.
- Run `make verify` before handing off implementation work or opening a PR.
- Never bypass hooks with `--no-verify`.
- Follow `docs/process/github-app-authentication.md`; commits must use the
  configured `Cesar-IA-Agent` identity.
